 "kind": "statement",
 "title": "Degree of the canonical bundle",
 "statement": "Let $k$ be algebraically closed and $C$ a\nproper smooth connected curve of genus $g$ over\n$k$. Then $\\omega_C=\\mathcal O_C(K_C)$ and\n\n$$\n\\deg K_C=2g-2.\n$$\n\n(*Stacks Project, Algebraic Curves, Lemma 53.4.1,\n[Tag 0BS2](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BS2), part (6),\n$\\omega_X=\\Omega_{X/k}$ for $X$ smooth of relative dimension one\nover $k$, together with Lemma 53.5.2,\n[Tag 0BS6](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BS6), parts (1) and\n(2), $\\omega_X$ invertible and\n$\\deg\\omega_X=-2\\chi(\\mathcal O_X)=2g-2$.*)",
 "source": {
